# Solve for Disappointment with Jace, the Mind Sculptor (a card, not a token) under Bot1's control: empower Jace's rule
# is that it won't put loyalty counters on a nontoken Jace planeswalker, so the spell makes its own Jace token and puts
# its one counter there, and the Mind Sculptor stays at three loyalty (CR 701.71a). Bot2 discards down to hand size on
# its own turn, so an Island is in its graveyard too.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Black Lotus
Island
Solve for Disappointment
Jace, the Mind Sculptor
Swamp
Swamp
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Llanowar Elves
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Jace, the Mind Sculptor.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Solve for Disappointment.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Llanowar Elves)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Jace Token.Token = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Jace Token.Counters.Loyalty = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Jace, the Mind Sculptor.Counters.Loyalty = 3
Bot2.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves; Island
